            <ArticleTitle>Elevated factor XIII level and the risk of myocardial infarction in women.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>287-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Factor XIII (FXIII) activity and antigen levels were determined in 955 patients investigated by coronary angiography. Patients were sub-grouped according to the presence or absence of coronary sclerosis (CS+, CS-) and a positive history of myocardial infarction (MI+, MI-). In females, but not in males, adjusted FXIII activity and antigen levels were significantly elevated in the CS+MI+ group compared to in the CS+MI- group. FXIII levels in the upper tertile were associated with significantly increased risk of MI in females, but not in males.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
